## How to review

Use `gh` for everything; you do NOT need to clone the repo.

1. Read the diff: `gh pr diff {{ issue.identifier }}` (or split by file with
   `gh pr diff {{ issue.identifier }} --name-only` and then `gh api`).
2. Check CI status: `gh pr checks {{ issue.identifier }}`. Mention failing
   checks if relevant, but don't block on them — review the code anyway.
3. Look at prior review context if needed:
   `gh pr view {{ issue.identifier }} --json reviews,comments`.

## Filing comments

- Inline comments on specific lines: `gh api` against the PR's
  `pulls/<num>/comments` endpoint. Anchor each comment to a `path` and
  `line` from the diff.
- Summary review verdict: `gh pr review {{ issue.identifier }} --approve`
  (LGTM), `--request-changes` (must-fix issues), or `--comment` (FYI / nits
  / questions). Pair the flag with `--body "<summary>"` describing the
  overall verdict.

## Done signal

Submitting any review records you in the PR's `reviews` list, which is
symphony's "you're done" signal — no labels to remove. Works for both
individually-requested and team-requested PRs (team requests don't auto-
clear, but your own review record does). If you genuinely can't review
the PR (e.g. need more context from the author), leave a `--comment`
review saying so; that still satisfies the gate.
